(Title) Tj
T*
(Preoperative intranasal dexmedetomidine for prevention of acute encephalopathy after major) Tj
T*
(joint reconstruction in older adults: study design and rationale) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Abstract) Tj
T*
(Acute postoperative neurocognitive dysfunction represents a serious complication affecting) Tj
T*
(morbidity and length of stay in elderly surgical patients undergoing joint replacement.) Tj
T*
(Sleep disruption and neuroinflammation are postulated mechanisms. The alpha-2 adrenergic) Tj
T*
(agonist dexmedetomidine exerts sedative, anxiolytic, and neuroprotective properties in) Tj
T*
(laboratory models. We present the protocol for a double-blind, placebo-controlled, single-) Tj
T*
(center trial evaluating preoperative intranasal dexmedetomidine for delirium prevention. A) Tj
T*
(total of 240 patients aged 60 or older scheduled for total hip or knee arthroplasty will) Tj
T*
(be randomized 1:1 to receive either dexmedetomidine \(100 µg total\) or saline via nasal) Tj
T*
(instillation the evening before surgery. Primary endpoint is delirium incidence assessed) Tj
T*
(by standardized cognitive screening within 72 hours post-op. Secondary endpoints include) Tj
T*
(delirium duration, severity grading, nocturnal sleep architecture, pain intensity, and) Tj
T*
(perioperative anxiety. Safety assessments include vital sign stability and adverse) Tj
T*
(respiratory events.) Tj
